" :answer-field/correct "b1b4a4ea-a7da-5796-ba31-4f54586baecf"] [:db/ensure "1aff7ca8-ae95-5320-870a-283e02efa317" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" :question/id #uuid "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880"] [:db/add "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix with $2$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/add "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{10} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=10=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 2 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n2+\\text{nullity}(A)=10,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=10-2=8.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 2. The number of pivot columns is 2, and the number of non-pivot columns is 8.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=8$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{rank}(A)=2$” is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$; $\\text{rank}(A)=2$."] [:db/add "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" :questi